  "body": "ES2015 Proxies introduce a potential security hole: a Proxy could be placed in the prototype chain of the global object, which could allow a same origin policy violation by allowing a script inclusion to read data out of another file by overriding the `get` trap.\n\nTo address this issue, @jswalden froze the prototype chain of the global object in Firefox. This has apparently shipped without any issue. TC39 standardized this with respect to the parts in ECMAScript in ES2016: https://tc39.github.io/ecma262/2016/#sec-immutable-prototype-exotic-objects . On the HTML side, Window.prototype and Location.prototype, as well as the global object itself, need to be \"Immutable Prototype Exotic Objects\" to get this frozen behavior.\n",
